## Deployment
https://todo-app-react-nl4v.onrender.com

## Discussion
- I decided to use the same React todo app that I used in exercise 1.15.
- I chose Render because I wanted to try this service. Previously I had experience with Vercel for Next.js apps.
- I had to modify the Dockerfile because I didn't want to deploy the Vite development server.

### Dockerfile
``` dockerfile
# used official node image for convinience 
FROM node:18-alpine 
# decided to keep with the same port as with Vite dev.
EXPOSE 5173

WORKDIR /usr/src/app

COPY . .

RUN npm install 
# previously it was just CMD with npm run dev -- --host
RUN npm run build 

RUN npm install -g serve

CMD ["serve","-s","-l","5173","dist"]
```

### Renderer
First, I created a new Web Service project on Render. According to the docs this is the way to deploy a Docker image.
When I pointed it to the repository, it gave me an error saying it needs to be an amd64 image. I built mine image on Mac M1, so I had to rebuild the image with this command:
``` bash
docker build -t todo-react --platform linux/amd64 .
```
After that I pushed it to registry and redeployed the app.
It worked.